{
  "version": "2.0.8",
  "changelog": "Speed pass on the 3D view (profiled first): the first-edit freeze is gone (edit data warms up in the background when a building lands), drags and steppers now update the picture lightly and settle after; picking rebuilt on the drawn footprint - every wall (front, back, sides) and every corner is grabbable; while a part is selected for sizing, pan and rotate pause and every drag sizes, with a banner showing the state; Edit this building is now a collapsible side panel and everything under the viewport scrolls; axis gizmo (X east-west, Z north-south, Y up) in the viewport's top-right; the view shows the surrounding streets, grass and neighbouring buildings in the game's colours; rotation and all numeric steppers turn the building live as you step - no Move / Resize needed; Detail Edit now says plainly that the Detail Editor works on roads and buildings are not supported there yet (nothing is sent); self-update and silent reporting built in.",
